+# Install a PP system in Boshsu
+
+Open **Performance → PP systems → Import ZIP / JSON**, choose the file, open its details, then choose **Use for this profile / world**. You can also drop the file in `PPProviders` beside `Boshsu.exe` and press **Rescan**. Importing never selects a system automatically or rewrites old scores.
+
+## Repository ZIPs and full calculators
+
+The first supported full calculator is **Akatsuki PP**, the exact Rust revision pinned by the Python wrapper used in the supplied bancho.py source. Download the [pinned Akatsuki repository ZIP](https://codeload.github.com/osuAkatsuki/akatsuki-pp-rs/zip/b96019f50aa7d09bcbde60016481a69df04315e4) and import it. No Python, Rust compiler, dependency installation, manual extraction or JSON editing is needed for the player. The import verifies the source tree and enables the application-shipped adapter; it does not execute code from the archive.
+
+Akatsuki is also included as an optional system in this private build. **Bosh PP remains the default.** Akatsuki has its own difficulty and aim/speed/accuracy/flashlight PP calculation. It does not add Bosh custom strain or Timewarp reward multipliers. Actual playback rate still changes difficulty once; MapLab timing/CS comes from the actual generated `.osu`. CS Changer, HD Remover, Maple strength and AC do not rewrite rated map difficulty. Only captured mod bits are supplied to the calculator, including RX/AP where present.
+
+The supplied **`ccv3-pp-main.zip` (CCV3 package 4.0.1)** is also supported directly. Leave it in `PPProviders`, press Rescan, open **CCV3 PP**, then choose **Use for this profile / world**. Its 223 source files are matched against the validated build. No adapter, compiler or dependency installation is required from the player. CCV3 uses its own complete algorithm, with no additional Bosh rewards. Existing scores are preserved when switching systems.
+
+Compatible rosu-pp 4-style Rust forks can reuse `engine/ccv3-pp/src/lib.rs` as a shared C ABI bridge instead of writing a new per-fork algorithm adapter. A developer must still build the dependency, pin its identity and validate it before a new source revision can be selected. The shipped managed map/live/result boundary is shared by Akatsuki and CCV3.
+
+Arbitrary Rust/Python/C++ PP repositories do not share a universal executable interface. Unknown or modified trees are reported as unsupported; import does not run repository scripts or load included DLLs. Completely adapter-free import of every possible repository is not implemented. A PP algorithm is always required, but the supported calculators are bundled into Boshsu, so no separate calculator installation is needed.
+
+## Simple formulas: one JSON file
+
+For a formula over Boshsu's existing rated attributes, create one UTF-8 file, for example `my-pp.json`:
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "myname.performance",
+  "name": "My PP",
+  "version": "1.0.0",
+  "calculation": {
+    "current": ["$bosh.current", 0.9, "*"],
+    "fc": ["$bosh.fc", 0.9, "*"],
+    "breakdown": { "My scale": [0.9] }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+This example returns 90% of Bosh PP. It is not a full replacement strain algorithm. `author` and `description` are optional. No manifest, manual checksum, compiler or capability list is required. Boshsu validates the formula and computes its identity. Formatting, property order and cosmetic metadata do not change its calculation checksum. Formula changes do: increment the version too.
+
+You may ZIP this file, including a GitHub-style wrapper directory and README/license. Legacy two-file packages (`manifest.json` plus `provider.json`) remain supported in folders and ZIPs. An archive must contain one PP system. Different versions may coexist; duplicate ID/version claims are rejected.
+
+The optional author helper packages an existing calculation object using the runtime validator:
+
+```powershell
+./stable-remastered/tools/New-PPProvider.ps1 `
+  -Module './calculation.json' -OutputFile './my-pp.json' `
+  -Id 'myname.performance' -Name 'My PP' -Version '1.0.0' `
+  -Author 'Your name' -Description 'Describe the intended calculation.'
+```
+
+This helper needs the documented source build tools. Players installing its output do not. It refuses to overwrite an existing file. The full expression input/operator reference is in [PP_PROVIDER_API.md](PP_PROVIDER_API.md).
+
+## Test before sharing
+
+```powershell
+./stable-remastered/tools/Test-PPProvider.ps1 `
+  -Provider './my-pp.json' -Beatmap 'D:/maps/example.osu' `
+  -Mods 72 -Timewarp 1.17 -Accuracy 99 -Combo 200 -Misses 1
+```
+
+`-Provider` accepts a JSON file, supported ZIP, legacy folder or `builtin`. The harness uses real map difficulty, reports the nearest representable integer-judgment accuracy, and never writes a profile or submits a score. Test NM/HD/HR/DT/NC, combinations, generated maps, runtime rates, misses/combo breaks, current PP, FC-at-current-accuracy and estimates.
+
+Provider selection is per immutable profile ID and local world. Historical values keep their ID/version/checksum; totals and best-play comparisons use matching systems only. Recent Plays retains the other history. A failed calculator preserves the raw score and an error, without inventing a fallback award.
+
+All providers currently retain Boshsu's existing local best-per-map/mode aggregation, `0.95^i` weighting and local bonus curve. Akatsuki's linked server has a different profile bonus policy; selecting its per-play calculator does not reproduce that server's entire account/ranking system. No offline result is server-authoritative PP.
