+# Boshsu offline PP API v1
+
+Status: Version 1.1 development. Built-in Bosh rewards and rate rules are unchanged. Custom providers never produce server-authoritative awards.
+
+Start with [the authoring/install quickstart](PP_AUTHORING_QUICKSTART.md). `tools/New-PPProvider.ps1` packages formulas with the runtime's own validator and generates their checksum. Pinned Akatsuki and the user's supplied CCV3 repository ZIP are supported by bundled calculators. Other code interfaces/revisions need build validation. See [the supplied Akatsuki PP inventory](STABLE_REMASTERED_AKATSUKI_PP_INVENTORY.md).
+
+## Installation and identity
+
+Use **Performance → PP systems → Import ZIP / JSON**, or copy a `.json` / `.zip` file or legacy provider folder into `PPProviders` beside the executable and Rescan. Installing does not change the active provider. Selection belongs to the immutable profile ID and local world. A score captures provider ID, version, SHA-256, API version, calculation policy and normalized-input SHA-256. Switching preserves historical files, XP and progression; totals/best-play comparisons use matching identities, while Recent Plays retains all history.
+
+A single JSON requires `id`, `name`, `version`, and a `calculation` object containing the programs below. Optional: `author`, `description`, `apiVersion: 1`, `ruleset: "osu!standard"`, `format: "bosh-expression-v1"`. Capabilities are inferred. SHA-256 covers canonical calculation JSON with sorted object keys and normalized numeric constants; array order is significant. No sidecar or manual checksum is needed. `examples/PPProviders/conservative.json` demonstrates this format.
+
+Legacy folders still contain `manifest.json` and `provider.json`; their original raw-byte module SHA-256 identity is preserved. The manifest supplies `id`, `name`, `version`, `author`, `description`, `apiVersion`, `ruleset`, `format`, `module: "provider.json"`, `sha256` and capabilities (`current`, optional `fc`, `estimates`, `breakdown`). IDs start with a lowercase ASCII letter and use lowercase ASCII letters/digits/dots/hyphens/underscores. `bosh.builtin` is reserved. Different versions coexist; duplicate ID/version claims are rejected.
+
+ZIPs can contain one single-JSON provider or legacy manifest/module pair, including wrapper directories and documentation. Imports inspect paths and bounds without extraction/execution, validate the copied staging file, then atomically publish it. Limits: 32 MiB archive, 4,096 entries, 128 MiB expanded total, 16 MiB individual source file; JSON keeps its smaller limits. Traversal/absolute/drive/backslash/alternate-stream/link/duplicate/case-colliding paths are rejected. Invalid imports leave no installed partial package. Rescan reads ZIPs directly; deleting a selected ZIP makes subsequent calculations unavailable instead of issuing another system's award.
+
+## Trusted full-map adapters
+
+`IFullMapPPProvider` is an internal boundary for application-shipped calculators: captured map/context → final score, disposable live estimator, and accuracy preview. It bypasses the Bosh baseline entirely. External expressions still receive summary fields only. No external archive chooses a native entry point or arbitrary DLL path.
+
+Akatsuki uses unmodified `akatsuki-pp-rs` commit `b96019f50aa7d09bcbde60016481a69df04315e4` (MIT). Its source ZIP is recognized by the SHA-256 of all 115 relative paths/file hashes, independent of wrapper folder/ZIP timestamps. Unknown or modified repository trees require an adapter. An optional `akatsuki.json` descriptor contains only `id: "akatsuki.standard"`, `format: "trusted-akatsuki-v1"`, and `sourceCommit`; it enables this exact shipped module, never code inside the package.
+
+CCV3 package 4.0.1 uses the unmodified 223-file user-supplied tree `4c79638f272b22d15a90c1a599e63856b60701029de68e411fa881a039a031da` (MIT). Archive SHA-256: `f64ffe044eefaa1f7513673ad542721b54dfd9bb70367031046efd4c0964b127`. No Git commit is inferred from a branch ZIP. Its optional descriptor uses `id: "ccv3.standard"`, `format: "trusted-ccv3-v1"`, `sourceTree`. Do not install both its ZIP and descriptor with the same provider ID/version; the catalogue correctly rejects duplicates.
+
+`NativeMapPPProvider` shares immutable context, provenance, estimate/live/result dispatch and safe native-handle ownership. The CCV3 C ABI can be reused by rosu-pp 4-compatible Rust dependencies; no formula or per-fork strain logic is reimplemented. A new fork still needs a validated build and pinned source/module identity. Arbitrary repository ZIP execution/import is not a universal calculator interface.
+
+CCV3 live PP deliberately uses the complete batch difficulty evaluator for the observed judgment prefix, cached by object count on the existing background worker (at most five requests/second). Its supplied gradual iterator omits custom tap-BPM/speed/marathon fields, which would produce different early-play values. The full-map FC-at-current-accuracy estimate and final result use the same complete evaluator. Cancellation is observed around native calls, not in the middle of upstream calculation. No PP parsing/calculation is added to the gameplay cursor owner.
+
+The owned C ABI verifies map MD5, standard mode, 16 MiB / 200,000-object bounds, pinned module SHA-256 and ABI. It parses map bytes once per prepared estimator and reuses full difficulty. Live prefixes reuse the parsed map and cache the observed prefix; upstream's old gradual interface lacks custom-rate support, so prefix difficulty is evaluated on its PP worker at the existing five-per-second maximum. NC includes DT; explicit actual clock rate replaces mod-derived rate once. Generated map timing/CS is authoritative; runtime CS Changer/HD Remover/AC/Maple cannot overwrite it. Akatsuki outputs no Bosh custom rewards. The adapter retains full numeric precision; the linked server rounds PP to three decimals separately.
+
+Map handles belong to one estimator and are released on disposal, failed preparation, stale-generation completion or shutdown. Cancellation is checked before/after bounded native calculations, not by interrupting Rust halfway through a call. Existing worker coalescing and stale-generation rejection remain authoritative. This is local calculation only. Profile aggregation remains the existing Boshsu policy, rather than adopting the linked server's distinct bonus curve.
+
+## Executable format
+
+External formula packages use bounded arithmetic JSON. Arbitrary WASM/native DLLs are incompatible and are never executed; the application-owned Akatsuki adapter is the separate trusted path described above. Programs cannot import code, loop, call functions, use reflection, access files/network/account data or see FPS/thread count. This smaller extension format fits the existing .NET Framework client without adding a native community-code runtime. It does not support arbitrary algorithms such as walking all hit objects; request a future API revision for unsupported attributes.
+
+Each output is a postfix expression. Numbers push constants; `$name` pushes an input. Operators consume their arguments and push one result. Binary operators: `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `min`, `max`, `pow`; unary: `abs`, `sqrt`; ternary: `clamp` with stack order value, lower, upper.
+
+```json
+{
+  "current": ["$bosh.current", 0.9, "*"],
+  "fc": ["$bosh.fc", 0.9, "*"],
+  "breakdown": { "Example scale": [0.9] }
+}
+```
+
+FC means full map combo, zero misses, current accuracy, same rated map/mod/rate context. Accuracy estimates evaluate the `fc` expression for 95%, 97%, 98%, 99%, 100%; they are hypothetical and provide no invented integer judgment counts. A provider lacking FC or estimates displays those features as unavailable.
+
+## Immutable normalized input
+
+`PPProviderInput` contains API version 1, `BeatmapMD5`, `PolicyVersion`, and a sorted read-only numeric `Values` dictionary. `ProviderPPCalculator.Normalize` is authoritative. Values use canonical rated map difficulty, never runtime CS Changer or AC as map CS. Baked MapLab timing comes from the actual selected file; `play.timewarp` is the separate runtime rate.
+
+| Fields | Meaning / units |
+| --- | --- |
+| `bosh.current`, `bosh.fc` | Existing qualified Bosh current and FC PP |
+| `bosh.base`, `bosh.fcBase` | Foundation PP before custom strain/rate contributions |
+| `bosh.aimBonus`, `bosh.speedBonus`, `bosh.extremeBonus`, `bosh.readingBonus`, `bosh.techBonus` | Explicit existing custom contributions |
+| `bosh.timewarpMultiplier` | Existing independent Timewarp reward multiplier |
+| `map.stars`, `map.aim`, `map.speed` | Rated difficulty attributes |
+| `map.cs`, `map.ar`, `map.od`, `map.hp` | Rated mod-adjusted difficulty, independent of runtime assistance |
+| `map.bpm`, `map.mechanicalBPM` | Rated BPM and measured mapped rhythm rate |
+| `map.duration` | Seconds |
+| `map.objects`, `map.maxCombo` | Full rated map counts |
+| `map.mapLabRate` | Provenance of baked map transformation; not an extra Timewarp multiplier |
+| `play.accuracy` | Fraction, 0–1 |
+| `play.combo` | Achieved maximum combo |
+| `play.misses`, `play.n300`, `play.n100`, `play.n50`, `play.judged` | Observed integer judgments; n300/n100/n50 absent for hypothetical estimates |
+| `play.mapTime` | Map milliseconds |
+| `play.mods` | Stable bitmask; HD Remover does not remove HD's rated effect |
+| `play.timewarp` | Physical runtime rate; DT/NC difficulty effects occur once in built-in Bosh |
+| `play.isEstimate` | 1 for hypothetical accuracy projections; 0 for score/live observations |
+
+Optional Bosh fields are absent when unavailable. Referencing an absent field fails visibly instead of inventing a value. Input normalization and formulas have no mutable gameplay/global access.
+
+## Output and bounds
+
+`PPProviderOutput` has `CurrentPP`, nullable `FCPP`, and an optional read-only `Breakdown` map (up to 16 entries). PP must be finite, non-negative and ≤1 billion. Intermediate magnitude ≤10^15; constants ≤10^12; power exponent magnitude ≤16. Each expression has ≤1,024 tokens and stack depth ≤128; the total operation budget is 16,384. Runtime checks enforce cancellation and a 20 ms worker-time budget (not a real-time scheduling guarantee). No expression executes on the gameplay owner. Existing live PP scheduling coalesces requests and rejects stale generations.
+
+Single JSON limit is 64 KiB; legacy manifest/module limits are 8 KiB / 64 KiB. At most 64 external files/folders are scanned. Duplicate keys, trailing data, excessive depth, unknown properties/opcodes, invalid API/ruleset, links, checksums and outputs are rejected. A failed provider keeps the raw local score and an error, with no false fallback award. Already-running work retains its immutable pinned provider instance during an idle rescan.
+
+## Author test harness
+
+From the workspace, run:
+
+```powershell
+./stable-remastered/tools/Test-PPProvider.ps1 `
+  -Provider ./stable-remastered/examples/PPProviders/conservative.json `
+  -Beatmap 'D:/path/to/map.osu' -Mods 72 -Timewarp 1.17 `
+  -Accuracy 99 -Combo 200 -Misses 1
+```
+
+Use `-Provider builtin` for Bosh. Mods 72 is HR+DT. The tool compiles trusted project code, reads the selected map, calculates real rated/Bosh attributes, validates the provider, and prints metadata, normalized input, digest, output and breakdown. It never creates a profile or submits a score. Since the score ABI requires integer judgments, the harness reports both requested and nearest representable accuracy; impossible accuracy/miss combinations fail. Omitted combo defaults to map maximum. Build tools and the pinned project PP libraries are required. Formula packages never load executable code; a full-map provider uses its pinned application-owned module.
+
+Automated provider tests are included in `tools/Test-Accounts.ps1`. They cover immutable input, worker/call-frequency independence, malformed manifests/programs/results, quarantine, pinned identity, profile/world persistence, history preservation and comparable rankings. Runtime/GUI evidence and remaining limitations belong to the Version 1.1 reports.
