+## Build from a source archive
 
-Run `tools/Build-Shell.ps1` for the x64 .NET Framework host and current Personal source assemblies. Run `tools/Build-Engine.ps1` for the separately pinned x64 native toolchain. The native build verifies the external frozen McEngine commit and JSON dependency hash. The current build uses already-present local dependency sources; a portable clean-machine bootstrap is still required.
+Keep the archive's `stable-remastered` and sibling `build/ultimate-migration/upstream/McEngine` folders together. Use Windows x64, Visual Studio Build Tools with MSBuild/Roslyn and .NET Framework 4.8 targeting support, CMake, and Python 3.12 or later. The native preparation script downloads and verifies the separately pinned MinGW compiler; it does not update dependency versions.
 
-Run `tools/Test-Contracts.ps1`, `tools/Test-Accounts.ps1 -Beatmap <fixture-path>`, `tools/Test-OfflineShell.ps1 -Preview development-44`, `tools/test_native_fixtures.py`, `tools/test_hosted_oracle.py` and `tools/corrective_checkpoint.py verify`. Stage each revision into a fresh destination; never overwrite an existing preview. Optional `--library-snapshot` and `--local-data-snapshot` accept the library and local account/results/replays from a closed preview inside this project. Test the staged DLL with `tools/test_native_abi.py --name development-44`.
+Extract the matching portable client into a separate folder to supply the existing pinned binary dependencies. Then, from `stable-remastered`:
 
-## Preview
+```powershell
+./tools/Build.ps1 -Runtime 'C:/path/to/extracted-client' -Python python -Jobs 2
+```
 
-`preview/development-44/StableRemastered.exe` is the Version 0.2.1 private development entry point. See [the corrective report](STABLE_REMASTERED_V021_CORRECTIVE_REPORT.md) and [quick guide](STABLE_REMASTERED_V021_GUIDE.md). Generated Map Lab difficulty is separated from runtime CS Changer/Timewarp, generated-file and live PP are corrected, and the existing profile supports editable names and full-size square portraits with Prestige styling. Offline Results opens automatically after completion, with green gains and red losses. Existing player history is preserved. Runtime settings/results remain mutable after the sealed checkpoint. Development-41 and its backups remain available; complete stable parity and public-release rights remain unqualified.
+MSBuild and CMake are discovered from installed build tools. Explicit `-MSBuildPath` and `-CMakePath` overrides are supported. `-SkipNative` builds only the managed host. Dependency restoration validates all binary hashes before copying and refuses conflicting existing files. The native build validates its complete pinned source inventory even without Git metadata.
 
-## Rights and attribution
+Outputs are `frontend/Bosh/osu!win/bin/x64/Release/StableRemastered.exe` and `_build/native/bin/StableRemasteredGameplay.dll`. These are build outputs, not a complete portable client. Stage into a fresh copy of the matching runtime, retaining its fonts, resources, required DLLs and qualified model. Never build over a running player installation.
 
-McOsu's GPL license and attribution remain in `engine/LICENSE`; upstream McEngine and utility notices are retained in their corresponding sources. Supplied Bosh source/assets, BASS, fonts, skins and runtime redistribution obligations are not assumed cleared. This is a private development preview; public release remains gated on the exact source/dependency/asset audit.
+## Validation
+
+```powershell
+./tools/Test-Release.ps1 -Runtime 'C:/path/to/staged-client'
+```
+
+This uses a disposable binary copy for contract, snapshot, layout, offline-shell, updater and allocation checks. It does not read a player's accounts or maps. GPU gameplay, physical input, audio and longer resource tests are separate qualification steps; a successful build or these CPU checks alone do not certify every feature or PC.
+
+Runtime updates preserve profiles, scores, progression, settings, maps, skins and replays. Diagnostics remain optional and bounded, with only the newest session retained. See [UPDATES.md](UPDATES.md), [PP_PROVIDER_API.md](PP_PROVIDER_API.md) and [PP_AUTHORING_QUICKSTART.md](PP_AUTHORING_QUICKSTART.md).
+
+## Source and rights
+
+Modified McOsu source and GPL notices are preserved in `engine`; McEngine and other upstream notices remain with their sources. Bundled fonts retain their licenses. This is an open-source derivative with separately supplied binary/resource dependencies. Historical Bosh PP is a supplied prebuilt module whose implementation source and redistribution provenance are unavailable here. Supplying source does not itself clear all supplied assets, BASS or other third-party redistribution obligations. Keep that limitation visible in release status; do not describe an unqualified package as a fully cleared commercial release.
